        "knowledge_point_id": "fabd8865-cc14-508a-aa81-4ba147f7f8d4",
        "knowledge_point": "Finding a General Expression for the Zeros of a Transformed Tangent or Cotangent Function",
        "problem": "Which of the following expressions gives all of the zeros of the function $f(x)=2\\operatorname{cot}⁡(x-\\frac{\\pi }{3})?$ Assume that $n$ is an integer.",
        "worked_solution": "The zeros of $y=\\operatorname{cot}⁡x$ are given by\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi ,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is an integer.\n\nTo find the zeros of $f(x)=2\\operatorname{cot}⁡(x-\\frac{\\pi }{3}),$ we replace the $x$ on the left-hand side of the above with $(x-\\frac{\\pi }{3}).$ This gives\n\n$$\nx-\\frac{\\pi }{3}=\\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi .\n$$\n\nSolving for $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x-\\frac{\\pi }{3} & =\\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi  \\\\ x & =\\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi +\\frac{\\pi }{3} \\\\ x & =\\frac{5\\pi }{6}+n\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the zeros are $x=\\frac{5\\pi }{6}+n\\pi ,$ where $n$ is an integer.",
